      "title": "💡 Tutor Tips | M3 Q2",
      "html": "<p>When you are asked to evaluate acceptance/continuance risks:</p><p>You need to identify facts from the scenario to consider how they impact the audit firm’s risks.</p><p>Then, as a part of the analysis, you should explain the importance of the facts in relation to the acceptance decision.</p><p>Use the seven procedures as a checklist to identify all of the issues relevant to the question.</p><p>If you are then asked for a response to those risks that would enable the firm to take on the client:</p><p>You must ensure that you can identify and explain how these acceptance risks impact the audit firm and be able to propose safeguards, where appropriate, to mitigate each risk or reduce it to an acceptable level.</p><p>You must also be able to identify when an auditor is unable to propose sufficient safeguards or is prohibited outright from undertaking the engagement.</p><p>You should start with identifying facts from the scenario that would affect acceptance risks and then explain how they affect the firm’s acceptance decision.</p><p>Once you have your answer, continue to the next section to review the facts you should have identified.</p>"
